    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>mod&lt;N&gt; is integer modulo 2^N over {+,*,^}. That is, it is a ring (mod&lt;N&gt;, *, +, ~, mod&lt;N&gt;(), mod&lt;N&gt;::max())</para>
<para>String literals for constructing common modulo equivalence classes are provided, e.g., 101_mod16 =&gt; mod&lt;4&gt;(5).</para>
<para>It is a lattice, i.e., totally ordered? </para>
    </detaileddescription>
